R = {
"Columbus reaches the Caribbean": ("PEW",3,"Columbus sailed west looking for Asia and connected two worlds that had been apart for 15,000 years.","With three small ships funded by Spain, Columbus landed in the Bahamas and then Hispaniola. The Taíno welcomed him; within decades they were nearly wiped out by disease, forced labor and violence.","The 'Columbian Exchange' swapped crops, animals and germs: potatoes and maize went east, horses, wheat and smallpox came west.","The Americas' languages, populations and religions today all trace back to this contact."),
"Treaty of Tordesillas": ("P",3,"The Pope helped Spain and Portugal draw a line splitting the non-European world between them.","After Columbus, Spain and Portugal agreed on a line about 370 leagues west of Cape Verde: lands west for Spain, east for Portugal. No one asked the people who lived there.","Brazil's eastern bulge fell on Portugal's side.","It's why Brazil speaks Portuguese and most of Latin America speaks Spanish."),
"Cabral claims Brazil": ("P",2,"Portugal stumbled onto Brazil on the way to India.","Pedro Álvares Cabral sailed wide into the Atlantic to catch the winds around Africa and hit the coast of Brazil.","Portugal built sugar plantations worked by enslaved Africans, and later found gold.","Brazil became the world's largest Portuguese-speaking country."),
"Balboa sees the Pacific": ("P",2,"A Spanish explorer crossed Panama and saw a second ocean.","Vasco Núñez de Balboa led an expedition through the jungle, guided by Indigenous people, and claimed the 'South Sea' for Spain.","Magellan crossed it six years later.","It proved the Americas were a separate continent between Europe and Asia."),
"Cortés lands in Mexico": ("PW",2,"Cortés landed with about 500 men and set out to conquer an empire.","Hernán Cortés defied his own governor, scuttled his ships so his men couldn't turn back, and allied with peoples who hated Aztec rule.","Within two years, the Aztec Empire fell.","Mexico's mixed Indigenous and Spanish heritage starts here."),
"Tenochtitlan falls": ("WP",3,"The Aztec capital, one of the largest cities in the world, fell after a 75-day siege.","Smallpox had already killed huge numbers, including the emperor. Cortés and tens of thousands of Tlaxcalan allies besieged the lake city and destroyed it block by block.","Spain built Mexico City on its ruins and ruled for 300 years.","Mexico City still sits on the old lakebed and sinks every year."),
"Pizarro captures Atahualpa": ("WP",3,"About 170 Spaniards captured the Inca emperor and toppled the largest empire in the Americas.","The Inca had just fought a civil war and been ravaged by smallpox. Pizarro ambushed Atahualpa at Cajamarca, took his ransom of gold and silver, and executed him.","Spain conquered the Andes and founded Lima in 1535.","Quechua, the Inca language, is still spoken by about 8 million people."),
"Potosí silver discovered": ("E",3,"A mountain of silver in the Andes funded Spain's empire and flowed to China.","Potosí's Cerro Rico was the richest silver mine in the world. Indigenous workers were forced to labor there under the mita system; many died.","Potosí's silver made the Spanish peso the first global currency.","Bolivia, home of the mine, is one of South America's poorest countries."),
"Manila galleon trade begins": ("E",3,"Spanish galleons linked Mexico and Asia, creating the first truly global trade route.","For 250 years, ships carried Mexican silver to Manila to buy Chinese silk and porcelain, then sailed back to Acapulco.","Chilies, corn and sweet potatoes spread to Asia this way.","It's the first time every inhabited continent was linked by regular trade."),
"Last Inca stronghold falls": ("WP",2,"Spain captured the last Inca ruler and executed him in Cusco.","The Incas had held out for 35 years in the remote jungle state of Vilcabamba. Spain captured Túpac Amaru and beheaded him.","Indigenous resistance went underground.","His name was taken up by rebels in 1780 and even by rapper Tupac Shakur."),
"Brazilian gold rush": ("E",2,"Gold in Brazil pulled in hundreds of thousands of migrants and enslaved Africans.","Explorers found gold in Minas Gerais. Portugal shipped huge amounts home; enslaved Africans did most of the mining.","Brazilian gold flowed to Britain to pay for imports, helping fund Britain's growth.","Ouro Preto's baroque churches are a UNESCO site."),
"Túpac Amaru II rebellion": ("WP",2,"The largest Indigenous revolt in colonial Spanish America shook the Andes.","José Gabriel Condorcanqui, an Inca descendant, took the name Túpac Amaru II and led tens of thousands against abusive officials.","He was captured and executed; Spain cracked down on Indigenous culture.","He's a national hero in Peru and an icon of resistance."),
"Haitian Revolution begins": ("WPI",3,"Enslaved people in the world's richest colony rose up and won their freedom.","Saint-Domingue produced much of the world's sugar and coffee using the labor of about 500,000 enslaved Africans. They revolted in 1791; Toussaint Louverture led them to beat French, Spanish and British armies.","Haiti became independent in 1804.","It's the only slave revolt in history to create a nation, and it terrified slaveholders everywhere."),
"Haiti independent": ("P",3,"Haiti became the first Black republic and the second independent country in the Americas.","After defeating Napoleon's army, Jean-Jacques Dessalines declared independence.","France forced Haiti to pay a crushing 'indemnity' for its freedom; Haiti paid for over a century.","Many historians tie Haiti's poverty partly to that debt."),
"Portuguese court flees to Brazil": ("P",2,"Napoleon's invasion drove the Portuguese royal family to Brazil.","British ships carried the court to Rio de Janeiro, which became the capital of the Portuguese empire.","Brazil gained schools, banks and a printing press, and won independence peacefully in 1822.","It's the only time a European empire was ruled from a colony."),
"Hidalgo's revolt": ("WP",3,"A priest's call to arms began Mexico's war of independence.","Father Miguel Hidalgo rang the church bell at Dolores and called on Indigenous and mestizo Mexicans to rise up. He was captured and executed in 1811.","The war lasted 11 years; Mexico won independence in 1821.","Mexico's Independence Day, September 16, re-enacts his 'grito'."),
"Argentina independent": ("P",2,"Argentina declared independence from Spain.","Delegates at Tucumán declared independence. José de San Martín then crossed the Andes to free Chile and Peru.","Argentina fought civil wars for decades.","July 9 is Argentina's Independence Day."),
"Bolívar wins at Boyacá": ("WP",3,"Bolívar's surprise march over the Andes freed Colombia.","Simón Bolívar crossed flooded plains and freezing mountains to surprise Spanish forces at Boyacá.","He created Gran Colombia and helped free Ecuador, Peru and Bolivia.","Bolívar is the 'Liberator' of five countries, and Bolivia bears his name."),
"Mexico independent": ("P",3,"Mexico won independence after 11 years of war.","Conservative leader Agustín de Iturbide switched sides and declared independence. He briefly made himself emperor.","Mexico inherited a huge territory but lost half of it to the US by 1848.","Mexico became Latin America's largest Spanish-speaking nation."),
"Brazil independent": ("P",3,"Brazil declared independence under its own prince.","When Portugal tried to reduce Brazil's status, Prince Pedro declared 'Independence or death!' and became emperor.","Brazil stayed united and kept slavery until 1888.","Brazil is the only Latin American country that became a monarchy rather than a republic at independence."),
"Battle of Ayacucho": ("W",2,"The last major Spanish army in South America surrendered.","Antonio José de Sucre's army defeated the Spanish viceroy in the Peruvian highlands.","Spain's mainland American empire was over.","It completed South American independence."),
"Gran Colombia breaks apart": ("P",2,"Bolívar's dream of one great nation broke into three.","Regional rivalries split Gran Colombia into Colombia, Venezuela and Ecuador. Bolívar died the same year.","Latin America stayed divided into many states.","Leaders like Chávez revived 'Bolivarian' ideas."),
"Mexico loses half its land": ("PW",3,"Mexico lost half its territory to the United States.","The Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo gave the US California, Nevada, Utah and most of Arizona and New Mexico.","About 80,000 Mexicans became US citizens overnight.","'We didn't cross the border, the border crossed us' is a saying in the US Southwest."),
"French invade Mexico": ("WP",2,"France invaded Mexico, and Mexicans beat them at Puebla.","Napoleon III used unpaid debts as an excuse to install an emperor. Mexican forces won at Puebla on May 5, 1862.","France took Mexico City anyway and made Maximilian emperor.","Cinco de Mayo is now celebrated more in the US than in Mexico."),
"Paraguayan War": ("W",3,"Paraguay fought Brazil, Argentina and Uruguay at once, and was devastated.","Paraguay's dictator López intervened in Uruguay and invaded neighbors.","Paraguay may have lost over half its population, including most of its men.","It's the deadliest war in Latin American history."),
"Emperor Maximilian executed": ("P",2,"Mexico executed the emperor France had imposed.","When French troops left, Benito Juárez's republicans captured Maximilian and shot him.","Juárez restored the republic.","It ended European attempts to rule Mexico."),
"Porfirio Díaz dictatorship": ("PE",2,"Díaz ruled Mexico for 35 years, modernizing it for the few.","Railways and foreign investment boomed; peasants lost their land.","Anger exploded in the 1910 revolution.","His motto 'order and progress' is a classic of development dictatorships."),
"Cuba ends slavery": ("P",2,"Spain abolished slavery in Cuba.","After the Ten Years' War and pressure, slavery ended.","Cuba's independence movement grew.","Afro-Cuban culture is central to Cuban identity."),
"Brazil abolishes slavery": ("PE",3,"Brazil became the last country in the Americas to end slavery.","Princess Isabel signed the 'Golden Law' freeing about 700,000 people.","Planters, angry at receiving no compensation, helped overthrow the monarchy a year later.","Brazil received more enslaved Africans than any other country."),
"Brazil becomes a republic": ("P",2,"Brazil's army overthrew the emperor.","A military coup sent Pedro II into exile.","The military kept a strong role in Brazilian politics.","Brazil's flag motto 'Ordem e Progresso' comes from this era."),
"Cuban War of Independence": ("W",2,"Cubans rose again against Spain.","José Martí, poet and leader, was killed early in the war.","Spain's brutal camps drew US sympathy.","Martí is Cuba's national hero."),
"Spain loses Cuba & Puerto Rico": ("P",2,"Spain lost the last of its American empire to the US.","After the Spanish-American War, Cuba became a US protectorate and Puerto Rico a US territory.","The US dominated the Caribbean.","Puerto Rico remains a US territory."),
"Panama splits from Colombia": ("P",2,"The US backed Panama's independence to build a canal.","When Colombia refused a canal treaty, US warships protected Panamanian rebels.","The US got the Canal Zone.","Panama took full control in 1999."),
"Roosevelt Corollary": ("P",2,"The US claimed the right to police Latin America.","Theodore Roosevelt added that the US could intervene to stop European meddling.","US troops occupied Haiti, the Dominican Republic and Nicaragua.","It shapes Latin American distrust of the US."),
"Mexican Revolution": ("WP",3,"Mexico's revolution was the 20th century's first great social revolution.","It began against Díaz and became a decade of civil war with leaders like Zapata and Villa.","The 1917 constitution promised land reform.","Mexico's ruling party governed for 71 years."),
"Panama Canal opens": ("ES",3,"The Panama Canal joined the Atlantic and Pacific.","US engineers completed it after France's failure.","Shipping between US coasts was cut by 8,000 miles.","About 5% of world trade passes through it."),
"Vargas takes power in Brazil": ("P",2,"Getúlio Vargas seized power and modernized Brazil.","He centralized government and built industry.","He killed himself in office in 1954.","He's called the 'father of the poor'."),
"Mexico nationalizes oil": ("EP",3,"Mexico took over foreign oil companies.","President Cárdenas expropriated US and British companies after a labor dispute.","Pemex became the state oil giant.","It inspired resource nationalism worldwide."),
"Perón in Argentina": ("P",2,"Juan Perón built a movement that still dominates Argentina.","With his wife Eva, Perón won workers' support with wages and welfare.","He was overthrown in 1955 and returned in 1973.","Peronism still shapes Argentine politics."),
"US-backed coup in Guatemala": ("PW",2,"The CIA overthrew Guatemala's elected president.","President Árbenz's land reform hit the United Fruit Company.","Guatemala fell into a 36-year civil war.","It fueled anti-US sentiment across Latin America."),
"Cuban Revolution": ("PW",3,"Castro's guerrillas took Cuba, creating a communist state near the US.","Castro and Che Guevara overthrew Batista.","Cuba allied with the USSR.","Cuba remains communist today."),
"Bay of Pigs": ("W",2,"A CIA-backed invasion of Cuba failed in days.","Cuban exiles landed and were defeated.","Castro moved closer to the USSR.","It humiliated Kennedy."),
"Cuban Missile Crisis": ("WP",3,"The world came to the brink of nuclear war over Cuba.","Soviet missiles in Cuba prompted a US blockade.","The missiles were removed.","It's the closest the world came to nuclear war."),
"Brazil military coup": ("P",2,"Brazil's army overthrew its president and ruled for 21 years.","The coup, backed by the US, ousted João Goulart.","Torture and censorship followed.","Brazil returned to democracy in 1985."),
"Che killed in Bolivia": ("WP",2,"Che Guevara was captured and executed in Bolivia.","His guerrilla campaign failed.","He became a global icon.","His image is on countless T-shirts."),
"Pinochet coup in Chile": ("PW",3,"Chile's army overthrew Allende on September 11, 1973.","Pinochet's dictatorship killed and tortured thousands.","Chile became a free-market laboratory.","Pinochet's legacy still divides Chile."),
"Argentina's Dirty War": ("PW",2,"Argentina's junta 'disappeared' up to 30,000 people.","The military kidnapped and killed suspected leftists.","Mothers of the disappeared marched weekly.","Trials continue today."),
"Sandinista revolution": ("PW",2,"Nicaragua's Sandinistas overthrew the Somoza dictatorship.","The US later backed Contra rebels.","The war killed about 30,000.","Daniel Ortega still rules Nicaragua."),
"Falklands War; debt crisis": ("WE",2,"Argentina lost a war with Britain, and Latin America fell into a debt crisis.","Argentina invaded the Falklands; Britain retook them. Mexico defaulted.","Argentina's junta fell; Latin America's 'lost decade' followed.","Argentina still claims the islands."),
"US invades Panama": ("W",1,"The US invaded Panama to capture Noriega.","Noriega was taken to the US for drug trafficking.","Hundreds of civilians died.","It was the last big US invasion in the region."),
"NAFTA; Zapatista uprising": ("PE",2,"NAFTA began, and Zapatistas rose up in Chiapas the same day.","Indigenous rebels protested free trade's threat to farmers.","They held autonomous zones.","The Zapatistas inspired global anti-globalization activism."),
"Chávez in Venezuela": ("P",2,"Hugo Chávez took power, launching Latin America's left turn.","Chávez used oil money for social programs.","Venezuela's economy later collapsed.","His successor Maduro still rules."),
"Argentina defaults": ("E",2,"Argentina made the largest debt default in history to that point.","Its currency peg collapsed.","Riots toppled the president.","Argentina has defaulted nine times."),
"Lula in Brazil": ("P",2,"A former union leader became Brazil's president.","Lula's programs cut poverty.","He was later jailed, then freed and re-elected in 2022.","He remains Latin America's best-known leftist."),
"Haiti earthquake": ("S",2,"An earthquake killed over 200,000 in Haiti.","It destroyed much of Port-au-Prince.","Aid poured in, with mixed results.","Haiti still struggles to recover."),
"Venezuela crisis deepens": ("E",2,"Venezuela's economy collapsed.","Oil prices crashed; hyperinflation followed.","Nearly 8 million fled.","It's one of the largest displacement crises in the world."),
"Colombia-FARC peace deal": ("P",2,"Colombia made peace with the FARC after 52 years of war.","President Santos negotiated the deal.","FARC disarmed and became a party.","Santos won the Nobel Peace Prize."),
"Haiti's president assassinated": ("P",2,"Haiti's president was killed in his home.","Mercenaries shot Jovenel Moïse.","Gangs took over much of the capital.","Haiti's crisis continues."),
"Milei elected in Argentina": ("PE",2,"A libertarian outsider won Argentina's presidency.","Javier Milei promised to slash the state.","He cut spending sharply.","It's a test of radical austerity."),
}
